    <string name="about_features">What it does</string>
    <string name="about_feature_scroll">Crown-style scrolling: direction follows the turn, distance follows how far you turned it; slow turns are close to 1:1 and reversing takes effect at once</string>
    <string name="about_feature_seek">Video position ring: in landscape it takes over the scroll and scrubs instead, also while paused; uses MediaSession for absolute seek when available, otherwise drags the player\'s own bar</string>
    <string name="about_feature_sensor">Independent of the input filter: HyperOS 4 disables it, so events are read from the zoom ring\'s optical sensor stream instead</string>
    <string name="about_feature_hot">Live tuning: feel parameters are read from system settings and apply in about 0.4 s, no reinstall and no framework restart</string>
    <string name="about_tech">How it works</string>
    <string name="about_tech_body">mt350x optical tracking sensor → crown model (re-anchoring, backlash ratchet, time-decayed peak speed) → single error signal driving the list → synthesized real touch events injected into the foreground window. The seek path prefers a reflected system MediaSession and falls back to dragging.</string>
    <string name="about_roadmap">Roadmap</string>
    <string name="about_roadmap_body">Keep filling in languages (Japanese, Korean, German); per-app gesture templates; more action types (zoom, paging, game skills); keep cutting battery and latency. Issues on GitHub are welcome.</string>

